{"answer": "Lore's agent pods run on the external floor (re-cinq/floor), not in Lore. The floor's own cluster agent runs each agent in a pod, and it installs the ai-agent-subsystem controller in its own namespace. No, Lore does not hold a Kubernetes client. CLAUDE.md says so directly: \"Agents run in pods of the external floor (ADR-049); Lore holds no Kubernetes client.\" Earlier, Lore's own Floor and a per-cluster `apps/cluster-agent` did hold or use cluster access (ADR-024, 2026-08-24). Those were removed on 2026-10-02. `apps/floor` was deleted, and so were Lore's copy of the controller, its cluster agent and the satellite chart.", "sources": ["CLAUDE.md", "adrs/ADR-049-external-floor.md", "adrs/ADR-031-agent-station-crds.md", "adrs/ADR-024-ubiquitous-language-execution-model.md", "specs/running-stations-in-any-k8s-cluster/spec.md", "docs/using-lore/platform-engineer.md"]}
